{
  "domain": "spec/corpus/semantics/domains/tally",
  "ruby_only": true,
  "spec": [
    "C2.3",
    "C6.1"
  ],
  "note": "Tally.Increase takes an argument named `count` — the same name as the field it increments — and its ensures reads `count.value == old.count.value + 5`. Per C2.3 an ensures resolves the settled state first, so with the count at 10 an Increase by 5 is accepted (15 == 10 + 5) and an Increase by 7 is refused EnsuresNotMet (17 != 15 + 5). Under argument-first resolution (C2.2, a given's rule) the same ensures would have compared the argument 5 with 15 and refused the first step.",
